/*
    Semi-additive inventory measures (requirement #6).
    Fact Inventory Snapshot: one row per product x warehouse x day.
    QuantityOnHand is additive across products/warehouses, but NOT across
    dates - a quarter's "stock" is the LAST day's balance, not a sum of every
    day in the quarter.

    Display Folder: "Inventory"
*/

Closing Stock :=
CALCULATE (
    SUM ( 'Fact Inventory Snapshot'[QuantityOnHand] ),
    LASTDATE ( 'Dim Date'[Date] )
)
-- Description: Stock on hand as of the last date in the current filter
-- context (e.g. "quarter-end stock" when filtered to a quarter). This is
-- the semi-additive pattern - CLOSINGBALANCE is the named DAX function for
-- it when working from a single fact/date combination:

Closing Stock (CLOSINGBALANCE) :=
CLOSINGBALANCELASTDATE (
    SUM ( 'Fact Inventory Snapshot'[QuantityOnHand] ),
    'Dim Date'[Date]
)
-- Description: Equivalent to Closing Stock above, using the built-in
-- semi-additive helper. Prefer this form - it's the documented idiom and
-- reads unambiguously as "don't sum across dates" to anyone editing the model.

Average Daily Usage :=
VAR DaysInPeriod = COUNTROWS ( VALUES ( 'Dim Date'[Date] ) )
VAR TotalShipped =
    CALCULATE ( SUM ( 'Fact Sales'[Quantity] ) )  -- units shipped in period, as proxy for usage
RETURN
    DIVIDE ( TotalShipped, DaysInPeriod )

Days of Inventory Cover :=
DIVIDE ( [Closing Stock (CLOSINGBALANCE)], [Average Daily Usage] )
-- Description: How many days the current closing stock would last at the
-- recent average daily usage rate. Standard supply-chain KPI built on top
-- of the semi-additive closing balance - never a straight SUM of stock
-- across the period.
